## Detailed Breakdown (computed)

Change any assumption above and rerun to see how these move.

| Item | Monthly | Annual |
|------|---------|--------|
| **Databricks platform** | | |
| SQL warehouse (15 analysts, $0.70/DBU) | {{sql_monthly}} | {{sql_annual}} |
| ETL pipelines ($0.15/DBU) | {{etl_monthly}} | {{etl_annual}} |
| ML training + serving ($0.40/DBU) | {{ml_monthly}} | {{ml_annual}} |
| Cloud infrastructure (50% of DBU) | | {{cloud_infra_annual}} |
| Storage (S3/ADLS) | {{storage_rate}} | {{storage_annual}} |
| Support (10% of DBU) | | {{support_annual}} |
| **Subtotal (infra)** | **{{infra_monthly}}** | **{{infra_annual}}** |
| Platform team (2 engineers) | | {{platform_team_annual}} |
| **Total with people** | **{{total_monthly}}** | **{{total_with_people}}** |
| | | |
| **DIY alternative** | **{{diy_monthly}}** | **{{diy_total}}** |
| | | |
| **Risk without platform** | | **{{total_risk}}** |

### Try it yourself

Change `turbines = 50` at the top and rerun. The storage drops,
the compute drops, the risk drops — and suddenly DuckDB + dbt
on a single server looks like the right call.

